# The installers the Windows golden image gets (misc/xen-vms/autounattend.xml,
# "Software installs"), vendored into the modified ISO by `make win_installers`.
#
# One per line: <file>  <sha256>  <url>. The target downloads each file ONCE
# into misc/iso/win-installers/ and verifies it with `sha256sum -c` before any
# image is built from it -- the check the Windows ISO already had, extended to
# what the answer file used to fetch at install time with no check at all.
# A mismatch refuses the build. It is never skipped: re-pin on purpose, by
# changing the hash here after looking at what changed, not by deleting it.
#
# Hashes recorded 2026-11-03 from what each vendor served that day, from the
# development container. The first `make win_installers` on Dom0 is the
# independent confirmation; a mismatch THERE means one of the two downloads got
# something else and the file must not be used until that is understood.
#
# Chrome has no versioned download URL, so its line pins today's file and a
# vendor update shows up as a refused build. That happened on the first Dom0
# run, 2026-11-04: Google's file had changed at 21:21 UTC on 2026-11-03
# (its Last-Modified), after the pin, and `make win_installers` refused.
# Re-pinned 2026-11-04 to the file Google served that day, downloaded on Dom0
# and in the development container, 171,970,560 bytes both, same sha256;
# its embedded version strings read 157.0.8089.0. No Authenticode check was
# possible here (no osslsigncode); two downloads agreeing is the confirmation
# this file's scheme provides. docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md, "make win_installers
# refuses the build". Since that day the target fetches from the lab's own
# mirror first (INSTALLERS_MIRROR in the Makefile, published by `make
# win_installers_mirror`), and the vendor URL below is where a file comes from
# when the mirror has none -- and the provenance of the hash beside it. A
# vendor's release then changes nothing until someone re-pins on purpose.
# .NET 4.8 and .NET 8 are pinned to
# the versioned files the vendors' redirects resolved to on that day (the
# runtime is 8.0.33); 7-Zip, Python, Acrobat Reader and the Office Deployment
# Tool were versioned already. Office itself is not here: the Deployment Tool
# downloads it from Microsoft's CDN by design.
